From: Security Fix <security@apache.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CVE-2021-25646: Prevent @JacksonInject values from being overridden by JSON input

The vulnerability allows authenticated attackers to override @JacksonInject
values (such as JavaScriptConfig) via crafted JSON input. By sending an
empty key "" with {"enabled": true} in a JavaScript filter payload,
attackers can bypass the druid.javascript.enabled=false security setting
and execute arbitrary code.

The fix overrides findInjectableValue() in GuiceAnnotationIntrospector to
explicitly set useInput=false on all @JacksonInject parameters, ensuring
they always come from Guice injection and never from JSON input.

Additionally, the JavaScript-enabled classes are hardened to validate
the config at construction time in addition to at use time.

---
